## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
Severity: MEDIUM  
AVGO is fab-lite, dependent on foundries like TSMC, exposing it to supply chain risks. Its revenue concentration in data center (e.g., Meta, Google) end-markets makes it vulnerable to capex cycles. While its ecosystem ties (e.g., VMware, Arista) provide some stability, the dependency on external foundries and cyclical end-markets elevates risk.  

